# {{.PascalName}}

1. Add the import `metapus/extensions/{{.Name}}` and `{{.Name}}.Register(reg)` to `extensions/register.go`.
   The server and `go run ./cmd/http-contracts` read this same module list.
2. Run `go run ./cmd/http-contracts` and `go run ./cmd/http-contracts -check`.
3. The migration is in `db/configuration/{{.Name}}/{{printf "%05d" .Version}}_{{.Table}}.sql`. It is embedded into the binaries and applied with the platform's by `go run ./cmd/tenant migrate`, which then creates the module's permissions (`{{if .Document}}document{{else}}catalog{{end}}:{{.Key}}:read`, `create`, …) from its registration and grants them to the admin role; assign other roles explicitly.
4. Add business fields to the model in `model.go` and their columns to the migration together; localize the presentation labels in `register.go`. Wire contracts are derived from the model: a field with `db` and `json` tags is writable, `meta:"readOnly:true"` makes it read-only, `json:"-"` keeps it off the wire. Rerun step 2 after changing fields.
5. Check `go build ./extensions/...`, tests and the generic list/form in the frontend.

Identity, table, route and hierarchy come from Definition. Do not add a second hierarchy flag.
Update requires version. Server fields (id, version, posting state) are never writable.
An entity that needs its own DTOs, references in responses or custom routes switches to an explicit registration (`v1.CatalogRegistrationFor`, see `internal/content`).
Before and Transaction hooks run in the mutation transaction. After hooks run only after the outer commit.
{{if .Document}}This is a header-only document. Add typed fields, domain invariants and MovementSource methods for its accounting registers. Register any new Visitor/Recorder in both HTTP and worker composition roots. CurrencyAwareDoc is optional.{{end}}
